title: "Eve's Law: The Reach Failure Codebook"
message: "If you use this scheme or dataset, please cite it and state the codebook version you coded against."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Hewan
    family-names: Tolera
    affiliation: University of Maryland
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hewanhtolera/eves-law"
abstract: >-
  A coding scheme and dataset recording AI deployment harms that existing
  law could not reach, and the regulatory instrument that would have reached
  each one. Six fields record the system's structural position, its effect on
  human discretion, the stakes and their bearer, the mechanical failure mode,
  the specific doctrinal element that prevented a remedy, and the layer at
  which a fix would bind.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - algorithmic accountability
  - regulatory design
  - deployment harm
  - liability
